// Section 3: amendments from the top-up read (changed behaviour at the freeze tip).
{"id": "B-AGENT-012", "decision": "02 §3.5 top-up (freeze tip fc5c1e78f)", "amended": "Agent runtime errors are recognised by cause and said in plain words with what happens next, never leaking technical text in the headline; exhausted credit beats HTTP 429; a free-tier limit (FreeUsageLimitError or 'Free usage limit reached') is its own cause, apart from a paid plan's usage limit, while a real provider rate limit (429), a rejected key (401), an oversized request (413) and a context overflow keep their own causes; missing/rejected keys offer sign-in recovery; terminal errors do not promise retry; every cause has Arabic wording.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "note": "top-up: test/agent_error_text_test.dart:13; test/agent_error_text_test.dart:82"}
{"id": "B-AGENT-121", "decision": "02 §3.5 top-up (freeze tip fc5c1e78f)", "amended": "Packages install into the app prefix with the agent daemon and Claude Code both pinned to exact versions (Claude Code at the same tested release the built-in Linux installs, never npm's latest); install records the versions of verified Node and both packages; removing keeps the Claude sign-in unless forget-sign-in is asked.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "note": "top-up: test/local_agent_runtime_test.dart:348; test/local_agent_runtime_test.dart:474; test/local_agent_runtime_test.dart:542"}
{"id": "B-SEC-097", "decision": "02 §3.5 top-up (freeze tip fc5c1e78f)", "amended": "The on-phone agent daemon runs as an ordinary user and is configured through its own settings before it runs (listen on loopback only, relay off, MCP injection into agents off, web UI off, dictation and voice mode off), then started with its 'daemon run' command; it never uses the launch flags newer Paseo refuses, never widens to all interfaces, never downloads speech models, and receives its password never as an argument and never traced.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "note": "top-up: test/local_agent_runtime_test.dart:411; test/local_agent_runtime_test.dart:626"}
{"id": "B-SEC-099", "decision": "02 §3.5 top-up (freeze tip fc5c1e78f)", "amended": "A plain project export leaves out every credential, private root folders such as .ssh, and every Git configuration file (repository config, worktree config, .gitconfig, of any size); a private export adds credentials, OpenCode data and the Termux migration exports kept inside Linux, but not logs; the file name says when private; credential names are recognised wherever they are.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "note": "top-up: test/manage_space/project_export_test.dart:43; test/manage_space/project_export_test.dart:62; test/manage_space/project_export_test.dart:95"}
{"id": "B-PROTO-071", "decision": "02 §3.5 top-up (freeze tip fc5c1e78f)", "amended": "Hello rejection: wrong or missing password reads as authentication failure, incompatible protocol is named plainly, unknown reasons are a plain disconnect, close code alone still maps; the handshake advertises rejection support and the password only when set; unknown frames are ignored; only daemon versions that were run live are accepted (0.9.2, 0.11.2, 0.12.0, 0.13.2, 0.14.0) and any other version, near neighbours included, is refused until it has evidence; Claude Code is accepted only at tested pins (2.1.283, 2.1.294, 2.1.316) and the catalog's Claude pin is always one of them.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "note": "top-up: test/paseo_hello_rejection_test.dart:130; test/paseo_hello_rejection_test.dart:146"}
{"id": "B-LINUX-126", "decision": "02 §3.5 top-up (freeze tip fc5c1e78f)", "amended": "Agent sign-in completes only after a signed-in probe; logout is verified; a check that could not run keeps a signed-in agent signed in; a list refresh asks an agent again only once its last answer is ten minutes old, and then the agent's own signed-out answer counts; a late older probe cannot complete a newer signed-out attempt; every sign-in check always ends.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "note": "top-up: test/phone_agents_controller_test.dart:1871"}
{"id": "B-LINUX-132", "decision": "02 §3.5 top-up (freeze tip fc5c1e78f)", "amended": "Unchanged installed pairs keep proof; a changed pin explains a check, but an older tested version that is still installed keeps running work while the update to the pin is owed, and only when nothing can run is the person asked for the check; a busy helper or running provider child blocks installation or update; running installs require continue; background loss exposes resume and restores the same component selection.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "note": "top-up: test/phone_agents_host_test.dart:473"}
{"id": "B-L10N-020", "decision": "02 §3.5 top-up (freeze tip fc5c1e78f)", "amended": "Tip and tutorial ids are unique, tutorials have 2 to 4 steps (the What's new walkthrough, which runs in its own sheet rather than as a highlight tour, is the one exception), and every tip and tutorial has copy in English and Arabic.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "note": "top-up: test/teaching_test.dart:163"}
{"id": "B-SEC-119", "decision": "02 §3.5 top-up (freeze tip fc5c1e78f)", "amended": "Private IPv4 ranges (10/8, 172.16/12, 192.168/16, link-local etc.) are private and their neighbours are not; IPv6 unique-local and link-local (with or without a zone suffix) are private; an IPv4-mapped IPv6 address is judged by its IPv4 part; only .local names count as private names, and a name that merely starts with a private address is not private; the CGNAT/tailnet range is not private for this rule.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "note": "top-up: test/browser_shell_test.dart:271"}
{"id": "B-LINUX-102", "decision": "02 §3.5 top-up (freeze tip fc5c1e78f)", "amended": "Projects still inside Ubuntu and repositories made there are exported including Git objects; the plan file frames one entry per line, and a name it cannot frame, or legacy project names that overlap, refuse the export instead of silently leaving files out.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "note": "top-up: test/manage_space/project_export_test.dart:212; test/manage_space/project_export_test.dart:228"}
{"id": "B-LINUX-112", "decision": "02 §3.5 top-up (freeze tip fc5c1e78f)", "amended": "A checksum mismatch stops before anything is unpacked; an archive without the program, a program that will not run, a program whose health check answers unauthorized (that does not prove it starts), or a failure after activation restores the previous program and link.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "note": "top-up: test/opencode_native_install_test.dart:359"}
{"id": "B-LINUX-152", "decision": "02 §3.5 top-up (freeze tip fc5c1e78f)", "amended": "A running server that does not answer is handled at launch: one rejecting our password is replaced, an old silent one is replaced, a young booting one is waited for, a young one that never answers is replaced once stale; a healthy server whose connect failed is simply connected again; a Stop that arrives during the launch health probe or while the launch password is saved prevents the replacement.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "note": "top-up: test/phone_server_healing_test.dart:1073; test/phone_server_healing_test.dart:1093"}
{"id": "B-LINUX-177", "decision": "02 §3.5 top-up (freeze tip fc5c1e78f)", "amended": "The usage collector helper starts only when something reads usage (starting the phone's OpenCode starts none), stays up while reads keep coming, stops after a quiet spell and starts again on the next read; one that runs is left alone; nothing starts when never set up, turned off or without the in-app Linux; turning off stops it and removes files, token and switch.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "note": "top-up: test/process_baseline_test.dart:85; test/process_baseline_test.dart:109; test/process_baseline_test.dart:147"}
{"id": "B-STATE-060", "decision": "02 §3.5 top-up (freeze tip fc5c1e78f)", "amended": "The profile sweep finds every per-profile key shape and nothing else: it matches the owning profile id in its place in the key, never a namespace word or an item id nested after another profile's id; a dotted id (a vs a.b, doomed vs doomed.agents) never takes another profile's keys; generated-interface, phrase-chip and agent display keys are swept while app-wide keys stay; deleting a profile leaves nothing keyed to it, nothing returns after restart, and deleting another profile leaves the first whole.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "note": "top-up: test/profile_deletion_test.dart:267; test/profile_deletion_test.dart:312; test/profile_deletion_test.dart:345; test/profile_deletion_test.dart:378"}
// Section 4: coordinator decisions (02 §3.6 day-1 amendments, 10 §20.3, 11 §9.3, NG22, review conflicts). Last, so they win.
{"id": "B-MIGR-004", "scope": "switch", "slice": 6, "module": ":android:migration", "decision": "ADR §9.9, D2, D3", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "amended": "Installing the native build over the Flutter build updates in place: same package name io.github.eslamasabry.opencode_mobile, signed by the signer of the lineage being updated (1DE5BF08…D60C for owner builds, 842284B2…1C for public releases), versionCode at least 10000, no uninstall, no data wipe."}
{"id": "B-MIGR-010", "scope": "switch", "slice": 6, "module": ":android:migration", "decision": "ADR §9.7, §9.8", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "amended": "Migration is one-shot and resumable: if the app is killed midway it resumes on the next start; re-running never duplicates drafts or prompts; the Flutter source data is never deleted in the switch release (source keys stay at least one release, files are never moved); a failed step shows a plain notice and leaves the old data untouched."}
{"id": "B-ANDR-068", "decision": "ADR §9.9", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "amended": "Android release resources are safe: no cleartext, adaptive/round/themed launcher icons, private and actionable background coding alerts, updates owned by the native AppUpdater (GitHub releases/latest, SHA256SUMS, same-signer check, PackageInstaller) with no Shorebird, bundled privacy policy naming sensitive surfaces, production signing lineage required, build identity exposed and shell approval authenticated, biometric lint exception narrow."}
{"id": "B-MIGR-012", "scope": "switch", "slice": 6, "module": ":android:migration", "decision": "ADR §9.9", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "amended": "Shorebird code push ends at the switch and the native AppUpdater takes over: it reads GitHub releases/latest, checks SHA256SUMS and the same signer, and installs through PackageInstaller; the app still tells the person a newer release exists and opens the install flow; when the update service is unavailable it never claims an update exists."}
{"id": "B-NAV-058", "decision": "NG1, D6; 02 §3.5 top-up", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "amended": "Search results hide what the server or device cannot open: in-app Linux has one Running on this phone; Linux Services is found only on the in-app Linux; backends lacking them drop catalog and project tools; OpenCode 2 keeps catalog; desktop gains shortcuts and loses phone-only results; without the shell its tabs are absent; AI setup is found by name when shared. (The OpenCode 1 and AI Team clauses are dropped; recheck by hand when the slice starts.)"}
{"id": "B-CHAT-122", "decision": "NG1", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "amended": "An approval ask is worded from the request alone: short shell commands show words and project, long ones the family their pattern saves or 'a command', OpenCode 2 apply_patch lists every path, absolute paths read relative to the project, and Delete only when every file is deleted. (The OpenCode 1 edit clause is dropped.)"}
{"id": "B-AGENT-229", "decision": "NG1", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "amended": "Choosing a chat agent for one OpenCode 2 chat leaves other chats and the profile default alone; it restores after restart and stays profile-specific. (The OpenCode 1 chat-agent path is not ported; recheck by hand when the slice starts.)"}
{"id": "B-PROTO-041", "decision": "NG1", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "amended": "Prompt dispatch supplies the caller's command ID. Where history confirms admission, only the exact user message ID confirms it (matching text with a wrong ID, session or role does not), paging is bounded, capability off refuses without lookup, and a closed connection cannot confirm. The OpenCode 1 history confirmation is not ported."}
{"id": "B-LINUX-124", "decision": "NG1", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "amended": "On ARM64 the phone server host hands off the pinned Node after root user bootstrap. No OpenCode 1 host is ever installed (NG1); recheck by hand when the slice starts."}
{"id": "B-BUILD-004", "decision": "NG1, D6", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "amended": "Action-coverage ledgers (Files, Lists, Models, Phone, Servers, Settings, Terminal, Tools): every mutating call and control has a recorded decision, every proof names a test that exists, every reachable control has a tap path, and the OpenCode 2 gateway sends the expected request. (The Team ledger and the OpenCode 1 gateway are dropped.)"}
{"id": "B-KIT-018", "decision": "D10", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "amended": "Frost appears only on the composer and the chat header: a RenderEffect blur on API 31+ and solid below that; strengths map to blur, saturation and tint, and saturation keeps grey grey; Saver, reduced motion or effects and high contrast keep surfaces solid; the stored choice is read once. No other surface turns to glass."}
{"id": "B-KIT-020", "scope": "after-switch", "decision": "D11", "reason": "Live backgrounds (aurora default) are ported after the switch or dropped"}
{"id": "B-KIT-047", "scope": "after-switch", "decision": "D11", "reason": "Policy for the animated live background; live backgrounds follow the switch (D11)"}
{"id": "B-STATE-020", "scope": "switch", "slice": 1, "module": ":engine:profiles", "decision": "02 §3.3 rule 3, D6", "amended": "Profile deletion removes the Memory pairing, token, key and outbox for that server only, even though Memory is not in the app; the keys are named by profile id so the sweep finds them.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01"}
{"id": "B-STATE-145", "scope": "switch", "slice": 1, "module": ":engine:profiles", "decision": "02 §3.3 rule 3, D6", "amended": "Profile deletion removes the last-known team record under its profile-scoped key, even though AI Team is not in the app; an unreadable record counts as no record and is still removed.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01"}
{"id": "B-SEC-075", "scope": "switch", "slice": 1, "module": ":engine:profiles", "decision": "02 §3.3 rule 3, D6", "amended": "The Memory vault passphrase stays in secure storage and is never written to disk or logged; it is deleted with the Memory data when the person deletes the server, even though Memory is not in the app. The native app never generates it or hands it to a node.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01"}
{"id": "B-SEC-176", "scope": "switch", "slice": 1, "module": ":engine:profiles", "decision": "02 §3.3 rule 3, D6", "amended": "Team-project editor drafts written by the Flutter app are removed by the profile deletion sweep, per target and profile, even though AI Team is not in the app; their secrets are never logged or restored.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01"}
{"id": "B-AGENT-193", "scope": "switch", "slice": 1, "module": ":engine:profiles", "decision": "02 §3.3 rule 3, D6", "amended": "Deleting a connection sweeps the built-in team engine data by its registered shapes (files/oc.teamEngine.<id>/, files/oc.teamEngineDeletion.<id>, oc.teamEngineAuth.<id>), even though AI Team is not in the app; the native app never attaches to or starts the phone engine.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01"}
{"id": "B-AGENT-301", "scope": "switch", "slice": 1, "module": ":engine:profiles", "decision": "02 §3.3 rule 3, D6", "amended": "Profile deletion removes stored team-project records (oc.orchestration.<id>.*, oc.team*.<id>) by their registered shapes, even though AI Team is not in the app, and nothing recreates them afterwards.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01"}
{"id": "B-AGENT-302", "scope": "switch", "slice": 1, "module": ":engine:profiles", "decision": "02 §3.3 rule 3, D6", "amended": "Profile deletion sweeps the team demo records by their registered shapes, even though AI Team is not in the app; no simulator is ever started.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01"}
{"id": "B-SEC-063", "scope": "switch", "slice": 6, "module": ":android:migration", "decision": "S02-7", "amended_at": "2026-11-01", "amended": "The native app holds no A2A credential. The v3 source cleanup erases every oc.a2aBearer.* secure entry together with the oc.externalAgents and oc.a2aTasks.* keys, and no late write can recreate them."}
{"id": "B-MEDIA-025", "decision": "10 §20.3, M3 / D10-1", "amended": "Model download is checksum-verified before the atomic install marker; partial responses resume only with matching Content-Range; corrupt or cancelled downloads never create a marker, and a cancel during download keeps the .part file for resume.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01"}
{"id": "B-MEDIA-007", "decision": "10 §20.3, M10", "amended": "Gallery and photo picking: photos are scaled down by the app before the bytes are attached; the gallery allows several up to the room left; one slot left uses the single picker; cancelling leaves nothing pending.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01"}
{"id": "B-MEDIA-008", "decision": "10 §20.3, §10.5", "amended": "Camera/picker requests are recorded before launch and selected bytes survive source deletion; cancel and denial leave no blocking photo; failed request persistence never launches the camera; after a lost native result and a restart the record's path names the capture file; a late result cannot resurrect a removed profile's photo; a pending photo blocks another picker; fake extensions and oversize images are rejected.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01"}
{"id": "B-MEDIA-031", "decision": "10 §20.3, §2.2", "amended": "The voice model manifest pins the vendored sherpa-onnx AAR by SHA-256 and version 2.0.1, RECORD_AUDIO is in the merged manifest, exact model values and totals hold, and the bundled notices are complete.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01"}
{"id": "B-MEDIA-032", "decision": "10 §20.3, §4.5", "amended": "On platforms without capture, the probe says unsupported, mic permission is refused, opening settings is a no-op; on Android the probe is the AndroidDeviceProbe binding, granted stays granted, a missing handler leaves it unknown.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01"}
{"id": "B-ANDR-013", "decision": "ADR §9.5, 11 §9.3, D11-2", "amended": "Coding alerts use the exact privacy-safe native contract. With live mode off, alerts are posted only for a run that reply watch holds after the person left the app (a short background service until the reply finishes); otherwise none is posted. A test notification ignores the live-mode gate but not platform permission; notification settings open once and failures are swallowed.", "amended_at": "2026-11-01"}
